From: kkutysllb <46704313+kkutysllb@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 20:30:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(markdown): merge cross-line emphasis and inline code to
 single line

Model output sometimes emits non-CommonMark cross-line ** emphasis and
inline code spans, which rendered as literal asterisks or broken code.
The parse pipeline now merges them back onto one line; fenced code
blocks are skipped. Carried by KCoder as upstream/0001 patch since the
upstream repo does not accept external PRs; this fork branch is the
long-term maintenance home.
